project OWNER_AWARE_GOVERNANCE:
  version 1
  title "Owner-aware goal and DAG governance"
  description "Adopt GitHub Issue #4 as an independent post-beta workstream. Separate authority to change the project goal or DAG from recommendation override MIG-08. Principal and owner-confirmation values are caller assertions, not authentication. Preserve preview-first mutation, candidate validation, optimistic locking, and safe-write controls. GOV_REQUIREMENTS completed 3p, GOV_AUTHORITY_CONTRACT completed 4p, GOV_DSL_CONTRACT completed 4p, GOV_INTERFACE_CONTRACT completed 4p, GOV_NORMATIVE_EXAMPLES completed 2p, GOV_DESIGN_ACCEPTANCE completed 2p, GOV_SOURCE_MODEL completed 5p, and GOV_AUTHORITY_CORE completed 5p on 2026-07-26, establishing a cumulative workstream-specific velocity sample of 29p/1d. Requirements fix the threat model, scope, defaults, write boundary, and non-goals. Governance semantics version 1 fixes actual-change classification and pre-change authority. Governance source contract version 1 fixes PrincipalId/PrincipalList syntax, Grammar 4 project fields, declared/effective defaults, source-preserving edits, project init/show behavior, unit-migration compatibility, and the digest-bound pre-change snapshot. Governance interface version 1 fixes an optional actor, repeatable accepted-by-owner assertions, operation-level batch confirmation, ProjectResult v3, MutationResult v2 with GovernanceDecision v1, PTGOV-101 under exit 1, and an atomic Grammar 4/CLI Contract 5 cutover. Normative governance examples fix defaults, preview, owner/delegate authority, missing/matching/wrong confirmation, same- and distinct-owner batches, pre-change self-authorization rejection, stale-digest composition, ordinary operations, atomic activation, and direct-edit guidance as one machine-readable acceptance baseline. Cross-cutting design acceptance traces all 10 Issue #4 criteria, all 15 interface invariants, the source and authority/write examples, nine explicit non-goal boundaries, and the implementation handoff with no open findings. Internal target Grammar 4 parsing, declared/effective metadata and source snapshots, formatting, project init/show/set and batch fields, unit-migration preservation, deterministic actual-change scope classification, caller-assertion normalization, pre-change owner/delegate evaluation, mixed-scope decisions, and PTGOV diagnostics are implemented without changing the active Contract 4 package root or CLI. GOV_CLI_PREVIEW completed 4p on 2026-07-27, bringing the cumulative workstream-specific velocity sample to 33p/2d. Internal target governed direct, batch, and advance planning; ProjectResult v3, MutationResult v2, and GovernanceDecision v1 projections; and the complete Contract 5 registry, text/JSON help, and usage recovery are implemented without exposing the active Contract 4 root or CLI. Subsequent tasks still own safe-write enforcement, editing guidance, atomic public activation, and installed acceptance. Release publication is outside this plan."
  as_of 2026-07-27
  duration_unit point
  velocity 33p/2d
  finish GOVERNANCE_ACCEPTED

resource DEVELOPERS:
  title "Implementation capacity"
  capacity 2

resource REVIEWERS:
  title "Normative and safety review capacity"
  description "Only one cross-cutting authority or public-contract review runs at a time"
  capacity 1

resource CLI_SURFACE:
  title "CLI, help, and result-schema ownership"
  description "Avoid concurrent changes to the shared command registry, help, and CLI projections"
  capacity 1

resource WRITE_PATH:
  title "Mutation and safe-write ownership"
  description "Avoid concurrent changes to governed mutation classification and write enforcement"
  capacity 1

resource DOC_SURFACE:
  title "Normative and guidance documentation ownership"
  description "Avoid concurrent cross-cutting edits to requirements, specifications, examples, and guidance"
  capacity 1







milestone DESIGN_ACCEPTED:
  title "Issue #4 cross-cutting design accepted"
  state reached




milestone CLI_PREVIEW_READY:
  title "Governed CLI preview and projections ready"
  state reached

milestone WRITE_ENFORCEMENT_READY:
  title "Governed write enforcement ready"

milestone GUIDANCE_READY:
  title "Editing guidance and generated warning ready"

milestone ACCEPTANCE_INPUT_READY:
  title "Owner-aware governance acceptance input ready"

milestone GOVERNANCE_ACCEPTED:
  title "Owner-aware goal and DAG governance accepted"












task GOV_WRITE_ENFORCEMENT CLI_PREVIEW_READY -> WRITE_ENFORCEMENT_READY:
  title "Enforce governance on every affected safe-write path"
  description "Enforce owner/delegate or accepted-owner assertions for goal and DAG writes, including atomic batch, import, advance, and governed metadata changes. Retain optimistic locking, candidate validation, symlink rejection, atomic write, and unaffected maintenance behavior."
  duration 5p
  priority 65
  requires:
    DEVELOPERS 1
    REVIEWERS 1
    CLI_SURFACE 1
    WRITE_PATH 1

task GOV_GUIDANCE DESIGN_ACCEPTED -> GUIDANCE_READY:
  title "Align editing guidance and generated project warnings"
  description "Update guide editing, README, and process guidance to state that direct DSL editing bypasses goal and DAG owner-confirmation checks, and align them with the generated project header owned by GOV_SOURCE_MODEL. Keep the statement guidance rather than technical enforcement."
  duration 3p
  priority 60
  requires:
    DEVELOPERS 1
    REVIEWERS 1
    DOC_SURFACE 1

gate GOV_WRITE_ACCEPTANCE_INPUT WRITE_ENFORCEMENT_READY -> ACCEPTANCE_INPUT_READY:
  reason "Acceptance requires all governed write paths"

gate GOV_GUIDANCE_ACCEPTANCE_INPUT GUIDANCE_READY -> ACCEPTANCE_INPUT_READY:
  reason "Acceptance requires aligned editing guidance and generated warnings"

task GOV_ACCEPTANCE ACCEPTANCE_INPUT_READY -> GOVERNANCE_ACCEPTED:
  title "Accept owner-aware governance across source and installed package"
  description "Run focused Core, grammar, mutation, CLI, batch, safe-write, help, guide, documentation, self-use, link, package, and installed-workflow tests. Verify Issue #4 defaults, delegation, confirmations, stale-digest behavior, ordinary mutations, direct-edit guidance, and all explicit non-goals."
  duration 4p
  priority 55
  requires:
    DEVELOPERS 1
    REVIEWERS 1
    CLI_SURFACE 1
    WRITE_PATH 1
    DOC_SURFACE 1
